Kylin NGCC Implementation Package

This package contains NGCC digital-signature implementations for the Kylin
submission.

Primary submission profiles (`q=2^64`):

- `Kylin-128`
- `Kylin-256`
- `Kylin-512`

Additional companion profiles (`q=2^24`):

- `Kylin-128-q24`
- `Kylin-256-q24`
- `Kylin-512-q24`

The reference implementation is portable C99. The optimized implementation
targets mainstream 64-bit PC processors with compiler and code-level
optimizations. In particular, `Optimized_Implementation/Kylin-128` includes
runtime-dispatched hash-path acceleration and reduced allocation overhead.

Current frozen packaged parameters are:

- `Kylin-128`: `q=2^64, h=62, d=7, h_vec=[8,9,9,9,9,9,9], BPORS=(K=4,B=7,t=128,k=6,mmax=95), w=17, len=33`
- `Kylin-256`: `q=2^64, h=65, d=8, h_vec=[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,9], BPORS=(K=9,B=8,t=66,k=5,mmax=187), w=16, len=66`
- `Kylin-512`: `q=2^64, h=64, d=8, h_vec=[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8], BPORS=(K=14,B=8,t=256,k=5,mmax=415), w=43, len=96`
- `Kylin-128-q24`: `q=2^24, h=22, d=1, h_vec=[22], BPORS=(K=2,B=12,t=864,k=7,mmax=90), w=6, len=52`
- `Kylin-256-q24`: `q=2^24, h=21, d=1, h_vec=[21], BPORS=(K=3,B=14,t=3072,k=8,mmax=202), w=6, len=102`
- `Kylin-512-q24`: `q=2^24, h=41, d=2, h_vec=[20,21], BPORS=(K=7,B=15,t=224,k=10,mmax=336), w=12, len=145`

The packaged NGCC wrappers accept messages up to `2^60` bytes, i.e. `2^63`
bits, matching the submission bound recorded in the specification.

Directory and File Inventory
============================

Top-level package files:

- `README`: this implementation-package manifest and build guide.
- `benchmarks/summary.md`: repository-local benchmark, stack, and section-size
  summary generated by `tools/collect_metrics.py`.
- `tools/bench_sig.c`: package benchmark driver used by each instance Makefile
  to measure key generation, signing, and verification on a 32-byte message.
- `tools/collect_metrics.py`: automation script that rebuilds instances,
  collects benchmark and memory metrics, and refreshes the paper data files.

Instance directories:

- `Reference_Implementation/Kylin-128`: portable ISO C reference
  implementation for the primary 128-bit classical profile.
- `Reference_Implementation/Kylin-256`: portable ISO C reference
  implementation for the primary 256-bit classical profile.
- `Reference_Implementation/Kylin-512`: portable ISO C reference
  implementation for the primary 512-bit classical profile.
- `Optimized_Implementation/Kylin-128`: optimized 64-bit PC implementation for
  the primary 128-bit classical profile.
- `Optimized_Implementation/Kylin-256`: optimized 64-bit PC implementation for
  the primary 256-bit classical profile.
- `Optimized_Implementation/Kylin-512`: optimized 64-bit PC implementation for
  the primary 512-bit classical profile.
- `Additional_Implementation/Kylin-128-q24`: companion
  implementation for the 128-bit classical profile with `q=2^24`.
- `Additional_Implementation/Kylin-256-q24`: companion
  implementation for the 256-bit classical profile with `q=2^24`.
- `Additional_Implementation/Kylin-512-q24`: companion
  implementation for the 512-bit classical profile with `q=2^24`.

Each instance directory listed above contains the common file inventory below:

- `Makefile`: builds `KAT_SIG`, `test_sig`, and `bench_sig`; provides `test`,
  `kat`, `bench`, `stack_usage`, and `clean` targets.
- `README.txt`: per-instance usage notes and ICCS helper-file provenance.
- `KAT_SIG.c`: unmodified ICCS digital-signature KAT driver for this instance.
- `test_sig.c`: local sign/verify self-test for the instance.
- `SIG_AlgorithmInstance.h`: NGCC SIG API declarations and instance-level
  length constants.
- `SIG_AlgorithmInstance.c`: NGCC SIG API wrapper implementation.
- `params.h`: frozen Kylin parameter constants for the instance.
- `context.h`: context type used to carry public seed material.
- `address.h`: address-field layout and address manipulation declarations.
- `address.c`: address-field layout and address manipulation implementation.
- `hash.h`: declarations for message hashing and pseudorandom generation.
- `hash_iccs.c`: ICCS-helper-backed hash and message-digest implementation.
- `thash.h`: declarations for tweakable hash functions.
- `thash_iccs.c`: ICCS-helper-backed tweakable hash implementation.
- `bpors.h`: BPORS+FP interface declarations.
- `bpors.c`: BPORS+FP signing and public-key reconstruction implementation.
- `wots.h`: WOTSCS interface declarations.
- `wots.c`: WOTSCS signing and public-key reconstruction implementation.
- `wotsx1.h`: one-address WOTSCS helper declarations used by tree code and
  benchmarks.
- `wotsx1.c`: one-address WOTSCS helper implementation.
- `utils.h`: utility declarations for tree and index operations.
- `utils.c`: utility implementation for tree and index operations.
- `utilsx1.h`: single-tree utility declarations.
- `utilsx1.c`: single-tree utility implementation.
- `merkle.h`: hypertree Merkle helper declarations.
- `merkle.c`: hypertree Merkle root and authentication-path implementation.
- `kylin_sign.h`: Kylin key-generation, signing, and verification declarations.
- `kylin_sign.c`: Kylin key-generation, signing, and verification
  implementation.
- `auxfunc.h`: ICCS auxiliary-function declarations copied from `docs/API_PKC`.
- `auxfunc.c`: ICCS auxiliary-function implementation copied from
  `docs/API_PKC`.
- `drng.h`: ICCS DRNG declarations copied from `docs/API_PKC`.
- `drng.c`: ICCS DRNG implementation copied from `docs/API_PKC`.
- `shake_offsets.h`: compatibility offset header retained from the upstream
  SPHINCS-style code layout.

Additional tracked file:

- `Additional_Implementation/Kylin-128-q24/timing_probe`: local timing probe
  retained for the `Kylin-128-q24` companion profile; it is not required by the
  NGCC SIG API build, KAT generation, or verification flow.

Generated files:

- `KAT_SIG`, `test_sig`, and `bench_sig` are generated executables.
- `output/` stores per-instance KAT output before it is copied to
  `Test_Vectors/`.
- `.stack-usage/` stores GCC `-fstack-usage` reports.

Generated files are not part of the source manifest. Run `make clean` in an
instance directory, or `make clean` from the repository root, before packaging a
source-only submission archive.

Build and Verification Commands
===============================

Run the full repository-local verification flow from the repository root:

    make verify

This refreshes parameter output, rebuilds all six instances, runs the
self-tests, regenerates the reference KAT files, and updates the package-level
benchmark and memory summaries.

Build all instances only:

    for d in Implementations/Reference_Implementation/Kylin-* \
             Implementations/Optimized_Implementation/Kylin-* \
             Implementations/Additional_Implementation/Kylin-*; do
        (cd "$d" && make clean && make && make test)
    done

Generate reference KAT vectors:

    for d in Implementations/Reference_Implementation/Kylin-* \
             Implementations/Additional_Implementation/Kylin-*; do
        (cd "$d" && make kat)
    done

Generated KAT files are stored in `Test_Vectors/`.

Refresh the package-level benchmark and memory summaries only:

    make metrics

By default this refreshes the primary submission profiles in
`Reference_Implementation/` and `Optimized_Implementation/`. To also include
the `q=2^24` companion profiles, run:

    python3 Implementations/tools/collect_metrics.py --include-additional

This updates:

- `paper/data/package_bench.csv`
- `paper/data/package_memory.csv`
- `Implementations/benchmarks/summary.md`
